258 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 225 0 R/E(Youth Service Corps Los Angeles \(YSC-LA\), funded by California Volunteers Office of the Governor, reflects a deliberate investment in the future of the City of Los Angeles. As part of Mayor Karen Bass\220s priority to Foster Opportunity, this initiative is designed to provide short-term employment, build a stronger workforce pipeline, connect opportunity to neighborhoods, and ensure that young Angelenos have meaningful access to careers that shape the future of Los Angeles.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

259 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 225 0 R/E(In 2025, 2,244 young people stepped into structured, paid work experiences that supported public service, community resilience, and essential city functions. At a time when many communities continue to navigate economic uncertainty and recovery, these opportunities matter deeply. Paid work experiences offer stability, professional exposure, mentorship, and a tangible pathway toward long-term economic mobility. For many participants, YSC-LA is not only a first job, but a first step toward seeing themselves as professionals, leaders, and contributors to the civic life of Los Angeles.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

260 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/P 225 0 R/T(This work is made possible through strong cross-department collaboration and the dedication of community partners who guide, supervise, and invest in young people every day. I extend my sincere gratitude to the teams who deliver these programs and to the Angelenos whose commitment, resilience, and talent continue to define the success of YSC-LA.)/E(This work is made possible through strong cross-department collaboration and the dedication of community partners who guide, supervise, and invest in young people every day. I extend my sincere gratitude to the teams who deliver these programs and to the Angelenos whose commitment, resilience, and talent continue to define the success of YSC-LA.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

261 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/P 225 0 R/T(The Mayor\220s Office of Economic Opportunity remains committed to expanding access, deepening partnerships, and strengthening YSC-LA as a scalable and equitable workforce strategy for Los Angeles. The momentum, built through partnership and collaboration, reinforces what is possible when we intentionally align opportunity with community need and invest in the next generation.)/E(The Mayor\220s Office of Economic Opportunity remains committed to expanding access, deepening partnerships, and strengthening YSC-LA as a scalable and equitable workforce strategy for Los Angeles. The momentum, built through partnership and collaboration, reinforces what is possible when we intentionally align opportunity with community need and invest in the next generation.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

