282 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H6/P 226 0 R/T(Youth Service Corps Los Angeles \(YSC-LA\) is a citywide workforce strategy designed to expand access to meaningful employment for young Angelenos while strengthening municipal capacity in priority service areas. Through alignment with Mayor Karen Bass\220 Foster Opportunity priority, YSC-LA connects youth to structured, skill-building work experiences that serve communities and build long-term career pathways.)/E(Youth Service Corps Los Angeles \(YSC-LA\) is a citywide workforce strategy designed to expand access to meaningful employment for young Angelenos while strengthening municipal capacity in priority service areas. Through alignment with Mayor Karen Bass\220 Foster Opportunity priority, YSC-LA connects youth to structured, skill-building work experiences that serve communities and build long-term career pathways.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

283 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H6/P 226 0 R/T(In Los Angeles, young people from low-income households, foster care backgrounds, or justice-impacted communities often face barriers to entering the workforce, including limited access to paid experience, professional networks, and clear pathways into stable careers. YSC-LA addresses these gaps by positioning employment as both an economic intervention and a workforce development strategy, ensuring that opportunity is aligned with community need and future labor demand.)/E(In Los Angeles, young people from low-income households, foster care backgrounds, or justice-impacted communities often face barriers to entering the workforce, including limited access to paid experience, professional networks, and clear pathways into stable careers. YSC-LA addresses these gaps by positioning employment as both an economic intervention and a workforce development strategy, ensuring that opportunity is aligned with community need and future labor demand.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

284 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H6/P 226 0 R/T(YSC-LA is implemented through a coordinated partnership involving the Mayor\220s Office of Economic Opportunity and key City departments, supported by a $22 million statewide investment through California Volunteers Office of the Governor. This investment strengthens Los Angeles\220 youth workforce infrastructure, enabling cross-department collaboration, expanded placements, and enhanced case management capacity.)/E(YSC-LA is implemented through a coordinated partnership involving the Mayor\220s Office of Economic Opportunity and key City departments, supported by a $22 million statewide investment through California Volunteers Office of the Governor. This investment strengthens Los Angeles\220 youth workforce infrastructure, enabling cross-department collaboration, expanded placements, and enhanced case management capacity.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

285 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 226 0 R/E(Participants are placed in structured, paid roles across City departments and community-based organizations. Paid interns contribute to high-impact initiatives such as green jobs and environmental conservation, food recovery and food security, education and tutoring, digital inclusion within public housing sites, public service operations, and skilled trade exposure in automotive equipment mechanic and warehouse toolroom internships.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

