endobj

305 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 227 0 R/T(The initiative operates within Los Angeles\220 broader youth workforce development ecosystem, working closely with YouthSource, FamilySource, and WorkSource Centers; the Los Angeles Unified School District \(LAUSD\); the Los Angeles Community College District \(LACCD\) and a consortium of experienced nonprofit service providers that serve as worksites.)/E(The initiative operates within Los Angeles\220 broader youth workforce development ecosystem, working closely with YouthSource, FamilySource, and WorkSource Centers; the Los Angeles Unified School District \(LAUSD\); the Los Angeles Community College District \(LACCD\) and a consortium of experienced nonprofit service providers that serve as worksites.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

306 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 227 0 R/T(Participants earn stipends or wages ranging from $17.87 to $25.00 per hour depending on program model, ensuring that work experiences are both meaningful and economically impactful. In addition to job placement, city departments provided professional development workshops and skills training to prepare participants for continued success in the workforce.)/E(Participants earn stipends or wages ranging from $17.87 to $25.00 per hour depending on program model, ensuring that work experiences are both meaningful and economically impactful. In addition to job placement, city departments provided professional development workshops and skills training to prepare participants for continued success in the workforce.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

307 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 227 0 R/T(Opportunity at Scale)/E(Opportunity at Scale)/Pg 13 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

308 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 227 0 R/T(The demand for structured youth employment in Los Angeles continues to outpace available placements. This year, nearly 8,000 applications were submitted for YSC-LA opportunities, underscoring both the need for paid work experience and the strong desire among young Angelenos to contribute meaningfully to their communities. This level of interest highlights the importance of maintaining and expanding access to high-quality workforce pathways across the City.)/E(The demand for structured youth employment in Los Angeles continues to outpace available placements. This year, nearly 8,000 applications were submitted for YSC-LA opportunities, underscoring both the need for paid work experience and the strong desire among young Angelenos to contribute meaningfully to their communities. This level of interest highlights the importance of maintaining and expanding access to high-quality workforce pathways across the City.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

309 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 227 0 R/T(The scale of participation and level of investment reflect the City\220s commitment to aligning opportunity with community need and advancing workforce equity at scale.)/E(The scale of participation and level of investment reflect the City\220s commitment to aligning opportunity with community need and advancing workforce equity at scale.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

310 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H5/P 227 0 R/T(Across all projects, the overarching goal remains clear: connect young job seekers to high-quality workforce programs that enable them not only to secure their first job, but to maintain stable employment and access long-term careers in public and community service, increasing their lifetime earning potential. To ensure continuous improvement, the Mayor\220s Office of Economic Opportunity tracks enrollment, completion, and participant outcomes, maintaining a data-driven approach that responds to the evolving needs of youth and the local labor market.)/E(Across all projects, the overarching goal remains clear: connect young job seekers to high-quality workforce programs that enable them not only to secure their first job, but to maintain stable employment and access long-term careers in public and community service, increasing their lifetime earning potential. To ensure continuous improvement, the Mayor\220s Office of Economic Opportunity tracks enrollment, completion, and participant outcomes, maintaining a data-driven approach that responds to the evolving needs of youth and the local labor market.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

