322 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 228 0 R/T(Youth Service Corps Los Angeles \(YSC-LA\) operated 16 programs across the City, including one high school\205focused initiative. While age eligibility ranged from 16 to 30, the majority of programs served young adults preparing to enter or transition within the workforce.)/E(Youth Service Corps Los Angeles \(YSC-LA\) operated 16 programs across the City, including one high school\205focused initiative. While age eligibility ranged from 16 to 30, the majority of programs served young adults preparing to enter or transition within the workforce.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

323 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 228 0 R/T(This year, 7,978 applications were received for opportunities across the City. The program placed 2,244 youth over a 12-month period, surpassing the original goal of 1,682 participants.)/E(This year, 7,978 applications were received for opportunities across the City. The program placed 2,244 youth over a 12-month period, surpassing the original goal of 1,682 participants.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

324 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 228 0 R/T(Of the youth placed, 1,280 completed 100 percent of their expected service hours. Program models ranged from 140 hours to 1,900 hours depending on the initiative. Based on completed service to date, participating youth worked an estimated 368,583 hours in communities across Los Angeles and earned approximately $9.4 million in wages and stipends. Final accounting is ongoing.)/E(Of the youth placed, 1,280 completed 100 percent of their expected service hours. Program models ranged from 140 hours to 1,900 hours depending on the initiative. Based on completed service to date, participating youth worked an estimated 368,583 hours in communities across Los Angeles and earned approximately $9.4 million in wages and stipends. Final accounting is ongoing.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

325 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 228 0 R/T(All 2,244 youth placed met low-income eligibility requirements. In addition:)/E(All 2,244 youth placed met low-income eligibility requirements. In addition:)/Pg 14 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

326 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1048 0 R/E(143 participants identified as justice-impacted)/Pg 14 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

