endobj

426 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/P 230 0 R/T(Through the Board of Public Works Office of Community  Beautifucation, the L.A. River Rangers continued to show the impact of youth leadership in climate and environmental stewardship. Corps members removed more than 140 tons of weeds, cleared 8,000 bulky items, and cleaned over 150 illegal dumping sites along the Los Angeles River, improving neighborhoods and restoring public spaces.)/E(Through the Board of Public Works Office of Community  Beautifucation, the L.A. River Rangers continued to show the impact of youth leadership in climate and environmental stewardship. Corps members removed more than 140 tons of weeds, cleared 8,000 bulky items, and cleaned over 150 illegal dumping sites along the Los Angeles River, improving neighborhoods and restoring public spaces.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

427 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/P 230 0 R/T(The team also supported fire season vegetation management, led volunteer cleanups in the Sepulveda Basin, and installed native plants near the LAX dunes. A total of 72 youth participated in the program, with 32 transitioning into employment after service, reinforcing the River Rangers as both an environmental force and a strong pathway into climate and public works careers.)/E(The team also supported fire season vegetation management, led volunteer cleanups in the Sepulveda Basin, and installed native plants near the LAX dunes. A total of 72 youth participated in the program, with 32 transitioning into employment after service, reinforcing the River Rangers as both an environmental force and a strong pathway into climate and public works careers.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

428 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H5/P 230 0 R/T(Behind the data are programs delivering tangible impact across Los Angeles. The videos below highlight how Youth Service Corps Los Angeles \(YSC-LA\) participants are strengthening communities through environmental stewardship and public service while building career pathways of their own.)/E(Behind the data are programs delivering tangible impact across Los Angeles. The videos below highlight how Youth Service Corps Los Angeles \(YSC-LA\) participants are strengthening communities through environmental stewardship and public service while building career pathways of their own.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

429 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/P 230 0 R/T(In 2025, the Department of Recreation and Parks continued to shine as a leader in Youth Service Corps, stewarding two impactful programs that are opening real doors for young Angelenos. Through City Pathways to Childcare and City Pathways for Youth, RAP not only provided meaningful work experience, but helped participants see long-term careers in public service and parks as a viable and exciting path forward.)/E(In 2025, the Department of Recreation and Parks continued to shine as a leader in Youth Service Corps, stewarding two impactful programs that are opening real doors for young Angelenos. Through City Pathways to Childcare and City Pathways for Youth, RAP not only provided meaningful work experience, but helped participants see long-term careers in public service and parks as a viable and exciting path forward.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

430 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H6/P 230 0 R/T(This year, City Pathways to Childcare supported 7 interns, with 6 transitioning into part-time employment at RAP or partner agencies after completing their internship. Meanwhile, City Pathways for Youth engaged 82 interns across parks citywide, with 20 moving directly into employment with RAP. These outcomes reflect more than placements; they represent a growing pipeline into careers in recreation, childcare, and community-based public service.)/E(This year, City Pathways to Childcare supported 7 interns, with 6 transitioning into part-time employment at RAP or partner agencies after completing their internship. Meanwhile, City Pathways for Youth engaged 82 interns across parks citywide, with 20 moving directly into employment with RAP. These outcomes reflect more than placements; they represent a growing pipeline into careers in recreation, childcare, and community-based public service.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

431 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 230 0 R/E(*Managed by the LA Conservation Corps, a contracted partner, members learn the importance of keeping our environment clean, gain leadership skills, and receive job training. )/Pg 16 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

