<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 232 0 R/Pg 18 0 R/A[1115 0 R 0]/K[11]>>
endobj

480 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 232 0 R/Pg 18 0 R/A[1116 0 R 0]/K[12]>>
endobj

481 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 232 0 R/Pg 18 0 R/A[1117 0 R 0]/K[13]>>
endobj

482 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 232 0 R/Pg 18 0 R/A[1118 0 R 0]/K[14]>>
endobj

483 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 233 0 R/E(The L.A. City Pathways program is an internship program designed to provide young adults with invaluable exposure to a wide range of career opportunities available in the City of Los Angeles. Participants earn the minimum wage and have the privilege of working closely with experienced City employees who serve as their mentors. This immersive program, led by the Mayor\220s Office of Economic Opportunity provides students with up to 750 paid work hours to support the operations of various departments through administration, project management, community engagement, and communications. )/Pg 19 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

484 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 233 0 R/E(L.A. River Rangers is a youth employment initiative serving young people ages 16\20526 who are committed to environmental stewardship and public service. Participants support the maintenance and enhancement of 18 miles of the Los Angeles River, contributing critical operational services across public paths, trails, and bridges within City boundaries. As the first program of its kind to provide coordinated services across the City\220s L.A. River public spaces, River Rangers strengthen both community infrastructure and workforce pathways in the green jobs sector.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

485 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 233 0 R/E(Designed as part of SB 1383, L.A. Community Composting and Food Recovery is an 800-hour job program that will hire Angelenos between 18-26 years old to maintain community composting sites and gardens, manage surplus food and food scraps, and prevent edible food from becoming waste. Participants are paid and trained in compost and soil management, native plants and species, OSHA 10, CPR/first aid, and other job readiness skills. Work crews support local food banks and food suppliers to deliver edible food to households facing food insecurity, diverting thousands of pounds of food waste from landfills as a result. This program provides hands-on skills development in an outdoor setting and offers opportunities to gain career certifications in the sustainability/green jobs sector.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

486 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 233 0 R/E(Wildland Firefighter Academy provides general training and work experience to prepare low-income and justice impacted Los Angeles City residents for entry-level positions in wildland firefighting and urban forestry. Over an six-week period, participants complete 320 hours of structured training and work experience preparation, including fire behavior education, safety protocols, physical conditioning, and teamwork exercises aligned with industry standards. Upon successful completion of the program, trainees receive a $3,000 stipend in recognition of their commitment and to help support their transition into employment opportunities within the field.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

487 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 233 0 R/E(The Pathways for Child Care program provides living-wage career opportunities for early childhood educators while expanding access to licensed child care facilities in Los Angeles. The program will provide 200-hour child care work experience and training. All participants  receive training in mandated reporting, CPR for infants and toddlers, and preschool curriculum. Practical experience is gained in lesson development and classroom management, and interns attend professional development workshops specific to the child care setting. )/Pg 19 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

488 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 233 0 R/E(The Los Angeles Regional Initiative for Social Enterprise \(LA:RISE\) Youth Academy is a 250-hour work experience program focused on improving housing, education, and employment outcomes for unhoused or housing-insecure Angelenos between the ages of 18-30. Participants will have the opportunity to get paid, via transitional employment at participating social enterprises. Placement sites include retail, social services, afterschool programs, facilities maintenance, information technology, education, entertainment, and the culinary field.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

