1506 0 obj
<</Title(The Mayor\220s Office of Economic Opportunity remains committed to expanding access, deepening partnerships, and strengthening YSC-LA as a scalable and equitable workforce strategy for Los Angeles. The momentum, built through partnership and collaboration, reinforces what is possible when we intentionally align opportunity with community need and invest in the next generation.)/Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1317 0 R/Prev 1485 0 R/Next 1519 0 R>>
endobj

1507 0 obj
<</Title(Deputy Mayor, Economic Opportunity)/Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1317 0 R/Prev 1520 0 R/Next 1486 0 R>>
endobj

1508 0 obj
<</Title(MAY 2026)/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1486 0 R>>
endobj

1509 0 obj
<</Title(Youth Service Corps Los Angeles \(YSC-LA\) is a citywide workforce strategy designed to expand access to meaningful employment for young Angelenos while strengthening municipal capacity in priority service areas. Through alignment with Mayor Karen Bass\220 Foster Opportunity priority, YSC-LA connects youth to structured, skill-building work experiences that serve communities and build long-term career pathways.)/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1487 0 R/Next 1521 0 R>>
endobj

1510 0 obj
<</Title(Our Approach)/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1487 0 R/Prev 1521 0 R/First 1522 0 R/Last 1522 0 R/Count -1>>
endobj

1511 0 obj
<</Title(For participants, this means gaining a first professional reference, understanding workplace expectations, and accessing pathways into public and community service careers. For neighborhoods, it means expanding local service capacity and reinvesting talent directly into the communities most in need.)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1489 0 R/Next 1523 0 R>>
endobj

1512 0 obj
<</Title(Participants earn stipends or wages ranging from $17.87 to $25.00 per hour depending on program model, ensuring that work experiences are both meaningful and economically impactful. In addition to job placement, city departments provided professional development workshops and skills training to prepare participants for continued success in the workforce.)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1489 0 R/Prev 1524 0 R>>
endobj

1513 0 obj
<</Title(Opportunity at Scale)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 1489 0 R/First 1525 0 R/Last 1526 0 R/Count -2/Next 1527 0 R>>
endobj

1514 0 obj
<</Title(City Pathways for Youth)/Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 1528 0 R/First 1529 0 R/Last 1530 0 R/Count -2/Next 1490 0 R>>
endobj

1515 0 obj
<</Title(Angeleno Corps is a service learning program where young adults work at community-based organizations while in school or on an educational program full-time.)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1490 0 R/Next 1516 0 R>>
endobj

1516 0 obj
<</Title(Members can support community organizations across focus areas such as education, environmental sustainability, food security, housing stability, economic opportunity, digital inclusion, healthcare access, and immigrant justice. Through these placements, participants build practical skills, strengthen their connection to their communities, and gain exposure to career pathways in the public and nonprofit sectors.)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1490 0 R/Prev 1515 0 R/First 1531 0 R/Last 1532 0 R/Count -2>>
endobj

1517 0 obj
<</Title(MAY 2026)/Dest[18 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1492 0 R>>
endobj

