<</Title(This year, 7,978 applications were received for opportunities across the City. The program placed 2,244 youth over a 12-month period, surpassing the original goal of 1,682 participants.)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1537 0 R/Prev 1542 0 R/Next 1561 0 R>>
endobj

1551 0 obj
<</Title(Youth contributed across multiple priority areas, often spanning more than one category, including public service \(1,040\), education \(902\), housing security \(131\), green jobs \(124\), food insecurity \(40\), and digital access \(27\). The gender distribution of participants included 63 percent identifying as female, 37 percent as male, and less than 1 percent selecting another gender identity option.)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1537 0 R/Prev 1562 0 R/Next 1543 0 R>>
endobj

